body:
I managed to reproduce this in multiple different ways:
* Following the steps above, I can reproduce this with `useSubThreads` both true and off.
* Instead of using `LoadThreadedGet`, instantiating a script object extending GodotObject also seems to cause a deadlock within the object constructor.
I struggled to get a MRP of this second issue until I came across this bug report and used a similar scene to load.

Here's a MRP that can (sometimes) reproduce the issue both ways. Check buttons are included to enable/disable certain actions.
[deadlock-mrp-scripts.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19171142/deadlock-mrp-scripts.zip)

![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8c7aad46-ee68-402a-bef2-43d087b89d15)

For context, the button calls the following method ():
```CS
public void Start()
{
    bool useSubThreads = GetNode<CheckButton>("%UseSubThreads").IsPressed();
    ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedRequest(
        ScenePathToLoad,
        typeHint: "",
        useSubThreads: useSubThreads,
        cacheMode: ResourceLoader.CacheMode.ReplaceDeep
    );
    GD.Print($"Load requested {(useSubThreads ? "with" : "without")} sub-threads [Status: {ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedGetStatus(ScenePathToLoad)}]");

    if (GetNode<CheckButton>("%InstantiateAfter").IsPressed())
    {
        GD.Print("Instantiating script...");
        var scr = new TestScript();
        GD.Print("Instantiated!");
    }
    if (GetNode<CheckButton>("%TryGetAfter").IsPressed())
    {
        GD.Print("Trying to get...");
        ResourceLoader.LoadThreadedGet(ScenePathToLoad);
    }
    GD.Print("Done");
}

```
The script being instantiated is an empty class declaration extending GodotObject.
```CS
using Godot;

public partial class TestScript : GodotObject {}
```
The constructor fails to return.
